AirliftFFI core — wholesale transplant from AirCard-iOS
--------------------------------------------------------
The entire device write path of this app (loopback tunnel connection,
RemotePairing session, AFC staging, AirTraffic sync, PosterBoard
injection, refresh writes, respring) is the AirliftFFI Rust core of
the AirCard-iOS project, vendored verbatim into `rust-core/`:

  Project:  AirCard-iOS
  Author:   Johnny Franks (Mak5er)
  Source:   https://github.com/Mak5er/AirCard-iOS
  Version:  v1.3.2, upstream commit
            40640c4d827aeab8d798285b57d24fcf6be070d0
  Path:     rust-core/ (crate `airlift_ffi`: src/, include/, vendor/)
  License:  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Johnny Franks

See rust-core/VENDORED.md for the vendoring record. The vendored
sources are unmodified; only the build wiring differs (the app links
the produced static library directly instead of packaging an
xcframework).

The app-side Grappa helper `Sources/App/GrappaHelper.h` /
`GrappaHelper.m` is likewise the upstream file, copied verbatim from
the same commit: the core resolves its `ALGetGrappaToken` symbol at
runtime (dlsym) and the helper tries a framework host session first,
then verifies each candidate from its built-in authentic token table
(kAuthenticGrappaTokens, also from AirCard-iOS) against a device
session before adopting one.

The Swift call layer (DeviceService.swift, TendiesFlash.swift)
mirrors the upstream app's TendiesEngine.swift call sites, arguments
and plist handling rule for rule.

